        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T18:40:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There have been a couple of threads on this and discussion about alternative with pros/cons (e.g. genrule). Given LLVM team request to avoid genrule, and that this is a build variant (which if accepted, we would remove the flag), in order to move forward, I feel strongly we do need this type of global change. It doesn\u0027t affect the normal builds and can be removed. Thank you.",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7462712c_e0ac89d1",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T18:52:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`linux_bionic_supported` isn\u0027t the right place for this, it is used by all modules that want to support running bionic on the host.  Where do you need this set besides bionic?",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1625e06e_f4217162",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003224
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T18:54:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "right now, they don\u0027t need this. but they\u0027ll need it when it comes to having the hack in \u003csys/user.h\u003e --- at that point all _users_ of bionic will need this. (though i do wonder if it should be _more_ global even than this in that case, because it wouldn\u0027t just be _host_ bionic.)",
      "parentUuid": "7462712c_e0ac89d1",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "033c9465_4acbed93",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T18:58:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was assuming that this flag would control the existence of the PAGE_SIZE macro, but that\u0027s not what aosp/2675944 does.  Is there a reason this can\u0027t just be `ifndef PAGE_SIZE`?",
      "parentUuid": "1625e06e_f4217162",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "290efa4e_40db69c8",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1889140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T19:05:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This C/C++ flag __BIONIC_NO_PAGE_SIZE_MACRO will be used in ART, Perfetto, etc. Basically in all the places where PAGE_SIZE is used.\n\nFor 4k targets, PAGE_SIZE will have the value 4096. For page size agnostic targets, PAGE_SIZE will have the function call getpagesize().\n\nIn nutshell, PAGE_SIZE is always defined.",
      "parentUuid": "033c9465_4acbed93",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "578ffb15_729a480d",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T19:07:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, PAGE_SIZE is still defined when __BIONIC_NO_PAGE_SIZE_MACRO is.\n\nOne thing though, we don\u0027t actually need to make any changes on host or set __BIONIC_NO_PAGE_SIZE_MACRO on host. It would be okay to set it on device builds only. We can completely ignore host things or keep them at 4k.\n\nIs there a place you would recommend Colin to set this for device?",
      "parentUuid": "033c9465_4acbed93",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a28fc261_3ef1b1df",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003224
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T19:10:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e For 4k targets, PAGE_SIZE will have the value 4096. For page size agnostic targets, PAGE_SIZE will have the function call getpagesize().\n\nwell, i assume assume you literally wouldn\u0027t set PAGE_SIZE _at all_ --- hence the name. (that\u0027s what glibc/musl and Apple\u0027s libc do.)",
      "parentUuid": "578ffb15_729a480d",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "973fab4f_610aafd2",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T19:16:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can whatever contains `#define PAGE_SIZE getpagesize()` also set `#define __BIONIC_NO_PAGE_SIZE_MACRO`?\n\nAlso, minor nit, `__BIONIC_NO_PAGE_SIZE_MACRO` is misleading as there is apparently still a PAGE_SIZE macro, it\u0027s just doesn\u0027t evaluate to a constant.\n\nIf this has to be set globally it should be done directly in Soong similar to aosp/2620545, but we\u0027d really like to avoid that if at all possible.\n\nFYI, Musl libc handles this by never setting PAGE_SIZE on arm64, and everything in the tree that compiles for host has already been \"fixed\" to not use PAGE_SIZE, e.g. aosp/2135646.",
      "parentUuid": "578ffb15_729a480d",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08279a50_1d20b170",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003224
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T19:18:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Can whatever contains #define PAGE_SIZE getpagesize() also set #define __BIONIC_NO_PAGE_SIZE_MACRO?\n\nno, because that\u0027s the whole point --- `__BIONIC_NO_PAGE_SIZE_MACRO` is like `_FILE_OFFSET_BITS`, telling bionic how to behave.\n\n\u003e FYI, Musl libc handles this by never setting PAGE_SIZE on arm64, and everything in the tree that compiles for host has already been \"fixed\" to not use PAGE_SIZE, e.g. aosp/2135646.\n\nindeed, and we may end up there one year, but during the experimental period, we don\u0027t want to affect innocent bystanders (ndk users in particular), and want _not_ having PAGE_SIZE to be opt-in.",
      "parentUuid": "973fab4f_610aafd2",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "72125ede_f3104b0d",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T19:19:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Aha! Thanks for the ref. Not defining PAGE_SIZE means every call site will need to be fixed, but that\u0027s okay.\n\nThen to answer Colin\u0027s question, we can\u0027t use \u0027ifndef PAGE_SIZE\u0027 because we aren\u0027t changing sys/user.h\u0027s default behavior. However, I do really like this suggestion if most parts of the codebase do \"#ifdef PAGE_SIZE\" because we would not need to go back and fix all those individual codepoints.\n\nStill, a global include would be needed so that sys/user.h could say:\n\n```\n#ifndef __BIONIC_NO_PAGE_SIZE_MACRO\n#define PAGE_SIZE 4096\n#endif\n```\n\n(or equivalent) The code referencing that should still use \u0027#ifndef PAGE_SIZE\u0027 for future compat.",
      "parentUuid": "a28fc261_3ef1b1df",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ddf892e7_be3f140f",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003224
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T19:20:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Aha! Thanks for the ref. Not defining PAGE_SIZE means every call site will need to be fixed, but that\u0027s okay.\n\nshort term i have no particular preference here (since it\u0027s opt-in anyway), but by the time this hits the ndk, i think literally _not having a `PAGE_SIZE` macro_ is the obvious choice.\n\n\u003e Still, a global include would be needed so that sys/user.h could say:\n\nexactly. that\u0027s why i liken this to `_FILE_OFFSET_BITS`.",
      "parentUuid": "72125ede_f3104b0d",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c6f3e5ae_fe2f57a6",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T19:36:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, if this affects `sys/user.h`, and is not going to be always-enabled for aarch64, then it unfortunately has to be a global flag.\n\nThere\u0027s a couple ways that could be implemented.  One is similar to aosp/2135646, although probably only affect device flags and not global flags.  I believe that also has to be done separately in Bazel, but should be exported to Make.  Another is to do it manually in `cc/compiler.go` inside `baseCompiler.compilerFlags`, which would then have to be done in both Bazel and Make too.  A third is to make this a new arch variant in `cc/toolchain/arm64_device.go` and add it to `arm64ArchVariantCflags`.  Then instead of setting a product variable to pass to Soong you would modify the `TARGET_ARCH_VARIANT` value in the product\u0027s `BoardConfig.mk` file.",
      "parentUuid": "ddf892e7_be3f140f",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "461615ee_b3249dab",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1889140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T23:04:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For Android U, I set up a global flag and configured it in bazel and soong aosp/2529029. I can do something similar.\n\nI will abandon this patch and add the product variable back here: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/bionic/+/2675944/10/libdl/Android.bp in order to submit the cl aosp/2675944",
      "parentUuid": "c6f3e5ae_fe2f57a6",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
